[b]QLC+ Swiss Knife v1.7.0 — build the Virtual Console[/b]

A new release of Swiss Knife, the free companion toolkit for QLC+ 5 workspaces (not affiliated with the QLC+ project).

The VC Visual Editor can now [b]build[/b] your Virtual Console, not only tidy it:
[list]
[*]Add buttons, frames, sliders, labels and CueLists; delete and duplicate.
[*]Wire widgets to functions from a list filtered by your naming groups — or drag a function onto the canvas.
[*]Drag widgets to move them, snapped to a grid.
[*]Rename, reorder and delete pages; choose the page QLC+ opens on.
[*]A label panel with your naming legend; arrange a frame's buttons by name group.
[*]Screen profiles (MacBook 1650×884, Full HD, tablet, iPad), optionally scaling the layout.
[*]Page templates: save a page, reuse it in the next show — buttons find their functions by name.
[*]Setlist CueList in one click.
[/list]

Everything is undoable, and your original show file is never changed — the result is saved as a new .qxw.

Download: [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/releases/tag/v1.7.0]GitHub release v1.7.0[/url] · [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/wiki]Wiki[/url]
